  "notes": "Worn by PH-CKA, PH-CKB and PH-CKC (airframes/MPH.json). Measured on PH-CKB's right side (2025-11-22, flipped; a 747-400ERF, the factory freighter's short upper deck: shapes/B744.json): 'CARGO' runs x 0.233-0.423 with its capitals about 1.9 m tall; on the right 'Royal Dutch Airlines' 0.117-0.179 then 'KLM' 0.181-0.218 under the crown; on the left the same block reads 'KLM' (0.117-0.154) then 'Royal Dutch Airlines', placed from PH-CKA's left side by proportion (that photo is too foreshortened to fit). The fin's 'KLM' spans 0.16-0.88 of the chord with its foot about 6.4 m up. The fin's 'CARGO' is gray on PH-CKB and PH-CKC, blue on PH-CKA: drawn gray. The winglets' 'CARGO' under the logo isn't drawn (titles can't sit on winglets). The 'Operated by Martinair' line and logos are read off small details (low). Each aircraft's name in small script under the cockpit, 'The Flying Dutchman' on the belly, the registration with its flags and the small 'BOEING 747-400ERF' aren't drawn. Colours by eye, KLM's blues as in KLM/standard.",
  "history": "New in the LAX round (2026-11-20): KLM Cargo paint on Martinair's freighters, drawn here for the MPH callsign."
}
